UNIT adopt_replace_block
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/lib/adopt.mts replaceUnmanagedBlock — the code is the truth, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG adopt_replace_block(existing: text, block: record[heading: text, startLine: i64, endLine: i64], managed: text, kept: list[text]) -> text
ENVELOPE existing, managed, block.heading and every kept element are well-formed Unicode text (no unpaired surrogate) of
  any content: empty, whitespace-only, LF, CR LF, lone CR or mixed line ends, any character. block.startLine and
  block.endLine are any integers of magnitude at most 2^53 - 1; a pair that is not a range of existing throws (R2), and so
  does a managed text that is not VISIBLE (R3). kept is a list, possibly empty, of any texts.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The `rdv init --adopt` splice: existing is a CLAUDE.md, block names the line range [startLine, endLine) that
  holds an unmanaged copy of a profile section, managed is the managed section that replaces it, and kept are the giver's
  rules no managed sentence represents. The result is the giver's text before the range, then managed, then (when any
  kept rule is VISIBLE) a new "Project rules" section, then the giver's text after the range — byte for byte outside the
  range except the blank lines at its two edges — the parts separated by one blank line in the line ending of the giver's
  lines outside the range.
BEHAVIOR
R1 LINES: existing is cut at every LF (U+000A); k LFs give N = k + 1 lines (the empty text is one empty line; a final LF
  leaves a final empty line). A CR stays part of its line; U+2028, U+2029, VT, FF and NEL are ordinary content.
R2 RANGE: S = block.startLine, E = block.endLine. Unless 0 <= S < E <= N the call throws. This check comes first.
R3 VISIBLE: a text is VISIBLE when it holds at least one character that is in neither WS nor CF; the empty text, and a
  text of only WS and CF characters, is not. If managed is not VISIBLE the call throws. block.heading is never read.
R4 EOL: list the lines OUTSIDE the range in order, lines 0 .. S-1 then lines E .. N-1 (BLANK lines included). EOL is CR LF
  when some line of that list OTHER THAN ITS LAST ends with a CR; otherwise LF. Lines inside the range never count, nor
  does a CR ending the last listed line: when E = N, a CR ending line S-1 is not counted. An empty list gives LF.
R5 A line is BLANK when every character of it is a space (U+0020), a tab (U+0009) or a CR; the empty line is BLANK. This is
  NOT the WS set: a line holding NBSP, FF, VT or U+3000 is content.
R6 BEFORE: let p be the last line index below S whose line is not BLANK. With no such line BEFORE is empty. Otherwise BEFORE
  is existing verbatim from its start up to and excluding the LF that follows line p; when EOL is CR LF one CR ending line
  p is excluded too, and when EOL is LF that CR stays as BEFORE's last character. The BLANK lines p+1 .. S-1 are dropped;
  trailing spaces of line p survive.
R7 AFTER: let q be the first line index at or above E whose line is not BLANK. With no such line AFTER is empty. Otherwise
  AFTER is existing verbatim from the start of line q to its end, including whatever ends it (a final LF or CR LF, a lone
  CR, or nothing). The BLANK lines E .. q-1 are dropped; indentation of line q survives.
R8 CONVERT a text to EOL: scanning left to right, each CR LF pair, each other CR and each other LF becomes one EOL (CR CR LF
  gives two EOLs, LF CR gives two).
R9 MANAGED: managed with its leading and trailing runs of WS characters removed (interior untouched; CF characters are not
  removed), then CONVERT.
R10 RULES: the kept elements in order, omitting every element that is not VISIBLE. With none left RULES is empty. Otherwise
  each remaining element loses the maximal run of CR and LF characters at its end (only those two characters: a space,
  tab or NEL ends the run), then is CONVERTed; RULES is HEADER, EOL, EOL, then those elements joined by EOL EOL. Nothing
  else is trimmed: leading whitespace, interior line ends and trailing whitespace other than CR and LF survive.
R11 RESULT: of BEFORE, MANAGED, RULES, AFTER in this order drop the empty ones and join the rest with EOL EOL. When AFTER is
  empty, append one EOL; otherwise append nothing (the result ends exactly as existing does). CITED FIDELITY package
PINNED charset WS = U+0009 U+000A U+000B U+000C U+000D U+0020 U+00A0 U+1680 U+2000-U+200A U+2028 U+2029 U+202F U+205F U+3000 U+FEFF CITED R3 R9 — ECMA-262 WhiteSpace plus LineTerminator, 25 code points; U+0085, U+180E, U+200B are NOT members
PINNED charset CF = U+00AD U+0600-U+0605 U+061C U+06DD U+070F U+0890-U+0891 U+08E2 U+180E U+200B-U+200F U+202A-U+202E U+2060-U+2064 U+2066-U+206F U+FEFF U+FFF9-U+FFFB U+110BD U+110CD U+13430-U+1343F U+1BCA0-U+1BCA3 U+1D173-U+1D17A U+E0001 U+E0020-U+E007F CITED R3 — General_Category Cf as of Unicode 17.0 (the authority's engine: node 24.16, ICU 78.3), 21 ranges; U+FEFF is in both sets; U+0085 (Cc) is in neither
PINNED text HEADER = "## Project rules (kept by `rdv init --adopt` — review and merge)" CITED R10 — adopt.mts line 136; — is the EM DASH U+2014, one character, between single spaces
INVARIANT MANAGED is never empty, so the result is never empty.
ORACLE value -> oracles/adopt_replace_block.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 dcb5ed208d8bc88026556b78450dde42727b02494fb3e4877a84fab2d4361fd0
SCOPE IN: R1-R11 over the envelope, both throws (the message text is not graded). OUT: locating the block
  (findUnmanagedDuplicate), choosing kept (extractKeptContent), the marker discipline of managed, any file I/O, the
  omitted-kept default of the real signature (kept is always passed here), and non-integer or non-number line fields (a
  js-only value; the real code throws on them).
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 (MIT), cli/lib/adopt.mts, function replaceUnmanagedBlock (lines 119-142); seam
  selfhost/seams/adopt_replace_block.mjs.
